  title "M1 Restore current Seal authority before continuing migration integration"
  description "Owner-directed all-Seal health recovery and bounded local focused V2-to-V3 migration correction. On 2026-09-25 the owner fixed the real upgrade path required consumer set to exactly battle-mechanics@3 for this slice. The bounded implementation is merged to remote main at fb9cd04a5825da1e4647e6922356f3f1dad24032: exact changed V2 source values are retained privately with SHA-256 digests and an aggregate 256 KiB limit; optional legacy meaning can defer only against that frozen consumer set; restricted original values are omitted from owner review; and the real upgrade route reaches a non-current review candidate without pointer or activation writes. The governed 112-test suite, typecheck, lint, build, SealGraph fsck, pull-request checks and post-merge main CI passed. Current-purpose plan, implementation, verification and inventory REFs were read back outside the stale frontier. This completes the authorized CS316 implementation slice and leaves zero internal implementation work for this slice. Realized end-user value remains zero because no candidate was accepted, activated or deployed; the verified contribution is local readiness for later owner and Stage flow. Do not activate a candidate, move a pointer, run paid provider calls, deploy, or claim migration complete. Full generation-bound capsule binding and atomic owner-accepted migration commit remain later authorized work. Preserve historical Seals and original proof scope; historical stale or draft counts need not reach zero. On 2026-09-25, after the merged-state and current-fit review was presented, the owner authorized this PERT reconciliation and resumption of cc304. The historical cc304 controlled trial remains stale evidence and does not complete the current task."

